ded) enables additional Indoor Air Quality functionality. Please refer to the Model 8920W Owner’s Manual for further information about thermostat features. NOTE: Refer to manuals for humidifier, dehumidifier, air cleaner, and ventilation products for recommended installation and operation. TABLE 3 – HUMIDIFIER SYSTEM SETTINGS System setting Description Factory default setting (bold) and setting range Humidifier Installed? Selects if a humidifier is installed. Yes/On HVAC is used for applications where the humidifier is installed on the HVAC duct. Yes/Standalone is used for application where the humidifier is independent of the HVAC system. (If set to No, no other humidifier settings will be available.) No Yes/On HVAC Yes/Standalone Display Button? NOTE: Only available if Humidifier Installed Yes is set to No. No Outdoor Temperature Select if outdoor sensor is attached or not. No Sensor Installed? Yes Humidifier Mode Selects auto or manual mode. Auto mode controls humidity based on the humidity setting and outdoor temperature. Manual mode controls humidity based on the %RH setpoint. (Auto mode is only available if Outdoor Sensor is set to Yes or Automation.) Auto Manual Allowed Humidifier Operation Selects when humidification is allowed to occur relative to heating and fan operation. Without Fan allows humidification to occur without the HVAC fan. This option should only be used when the humidifier is independent of the HVAC system. NOTE: Without Fan is only available when Humidifier Installed is set to Yes/ Standalone. Heat Only Heat or Fan Forces Fan Without Fan CAUTION: When Humidifier Operation is set to Without Fan the thermostat will turn on humidification without energizing the HVAC fan. Do not select this option when the humidifier is installed on the HVAC duct. Without airflow moisture can accumulate in the duct resulting in significant damage. TABLE 3 – HUMIDIFIER SYSTEM SETTINGS System setting Humidity Deadband Description Select the minimum difference bet